# `uv run` byproduct. This repo builds with hatchling and CI installs with
# pip; uv is only ever a local convenience runner, so a lockfile here would
# declare a toolchain the project does not actually use.
uv.lock
# tree-sitter build outputs (`tree-sitter generate`) and VS Code extension installs (issue #254)
editors/tree-sitter-lnpl/src/
editors/vscode/node_modules/
# coverage.py data and reports (issue #247) — the coverage CI job uploads them as an artifact
/.coverage
/.coverage.*
/coverage.xml
/coverage.json
/htmlcov/
